{"id":565,"date":"2020-10-29T12:24:55","date_gmt":"2020-10-29T19:24:55","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=565"},"modified":"2024-08-30T10:04:29","modified_gmt":"2024-08-30T17:04:29","slug":"conditionals","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/conditionals\/","title":{"rendered":"1E: Conditionals"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ea714ca\" name=\"6a2213ea714ca\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Getting Started<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Make sure that your CoDrone Mini is paired before starting the lesson! If you forgot how to do this, make sure to review how to pair to Blockly <a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/cdmb-pairing\/\">here<\/a>.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ea71639\" name=\"6a2213ea71639\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are conditionals?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Conditionals are statements that help programs make decisions depending on if the statement is true or false. In Blockly, conditionals include if, else if, and else statements. You actually use conditionals to make decisions in your own life!<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Some examples:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If it\u2019s sunny, I\u2019ll play outside.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If my alarm goes off, I\u2019ll wake up. Else, I\u2019ll sleep in.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ea716c0\" name=\"6a2213ea716c0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>If statements<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The if statement block is in the light purple logic menu and has two parts. The first part is the notch next to the if, and this is where you would put the condition. This is the &#8220;if _____&#8221; part of an if statement. What you put in this space can only be true or false. Some examples include:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the up button is pressed<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If 2 is even<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the battery percentage is less than 25<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The space beneath condition is where you include the &#8220;then _____&#8221; part of the statement, and is the action you want to be performed if the condition is true. You can do this by finding the block you need in the menus, and then dragging and dropping it into that space so the blocks connect.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;566&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;567&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ea7171b\" name=\"6a2213ea7171b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program an if statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You have everything you need to program your first if statement! Program your drone to take off and then fly forward for 2 seconds if 5 is less than 10. You can find an equation block in the light purple logic menu, and you can select inequality signs from the drop-down menu. Number blocks are in the gray math menu. Don\u2019t forget to have your drone land!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;566&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;570&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;571&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Next, use the same program but switch the less than sign to a greater than sign&#8230;just to see what happens!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;572&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ea7178a\" name=\"6a2213ea7178a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Else statements<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">There might be times when you want your program to do one thing if the condition is true and a completely different thing if the condition is false. In those cases, you would use an else statement, which is part of the if statement block. Just click on the blue gear icon and then drag and connect the else block to the if statement block. Else statements are usually written as &#8220;If _____, then ______. Else, _____.&#8221;<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;573&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;574&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The first part of the else statement block looks just like an if statement! There&#8217;s a space for your condition and another space for what happens when your condition is true. The second part of the else statement is for what happens when your condition is false. To include that action, find the block you need in the menus, and then drag and drop it into the space next to the else so the blocks connect.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;576&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is how an else statement works once you run it:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your program will check the if part of the statement. If the condition is true, it will run the code within the if statement, and once that&#8217;s finished, your program will run the code after the if statement.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is false, your program will run the code within the else statement, and once that&#8217;s finished, your program will run the code after the else statement.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ea717d5\" name=\"6a2213ea717d5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program an else statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Program your drone to take off and then so that if pi, which is in the gray math menu under its symbol, is greater than 3, it will turn left for 3 seconds. Else, it will fly backward for 2 seconds.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;577&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ea71845\" name=\"6a2213ea71845\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Else if statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sometimes you might want to have more than two options when making a decision. If that is the case, you can use an else if statement between your if and else statements.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To use an else if statement, click on the blue gear icon in the if statement block from the light purple logic menu, and then drag the else if block to the if block. You\u2019ll see that just like an if statement block, there is a notch for your conditional and then a space for what will happen if the condition is true.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;578&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is how an else statement works once you run it:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your program will check the if part of the statement. If the condition is true, it will run the code within the if statement, and once that&#8217;s finished, your program will run the code after the if statement.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is false, your program will move on to the else if statement. If the condition is true, it will run the code within the else if statement, and once that\u2019s finished, your program will run the code after the else if statement.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is false, your program will run the code within the else statement, and once that&#8217;s finished, your program will run the code after the else statement.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can have as many else if statements as you want in a program! Just remember there should always be a beginning if statement.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ea71892\" name=\"6a2213ea71892\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program an else if statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Program your drone so that if 7 is an even number, your CoDrone Mini will fly forward, hover, and then fly left. Else, if 8 is an even number, your CoDrone Mini will turn right for 3 seconds. Else, your CoDrone Mini will fly backward for 1 second.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;579&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">After testing this version out, use the drop-down menus to change your options. What happens when you set both numbers to odd, or when 7 is even and 8 is odd?<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;580&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;581&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ea718f8\" name=\"6a2213ea718f8\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: CoDrone Calculator<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Get your CoDrone to do your math for you! Program your CoDrone to fly in different patterns based on if the mathematical equations you answer are true or false.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Rules:<\/b><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You must use at least one if statement and one else statement.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Don\u2019t forget an emergency stop!<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hint:<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">There are blocks that are more complex than the number block. If you want to use these in an equation, drag the light purple equation block to your workspace and then drag the block you need into one of those blank spaces.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;582&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 10 Getting Started [vc_column_text]Make sure that your CoDrone Mini is paired before starting the lesson! If you forgot how to do this, make sure to review how to&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/conditionals\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1687,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":true,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":407,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1760,1817,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,2125,2119,2123,2124,2122],"class_list":["post-565","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-conditionals","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-junior","lesson-tag-programming","module-junior","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/565","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":10,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/565\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12815,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/565\/revisions\/1